  "result": "I implemented `satisfies(version, range)` in `src/semver.js` following `docs/SPEC.md`, and `npm test` passes (10 of 10).\n\nI added `test/satisfies.test.js`, which covers each section of the spec:\n- comparators and whitespace\n- version ordering\n- x-ranges and partial versions\n- tilde, caret and hyphen ranges\n- `||` and AND sets\n- the prerelease rule\n- invalid inputs returning `false` instead of throwing\n\nThe spec leaves a few cases open. These are the choices I made:\n- **Wildcard then number:** a range like `1.x.3` is invalid and returns `false`.\n- **Fully wild with `>` or `<`:** `>*` and `<*` match nothing.\n- **Operators on `~` and `^`:** `~` and `^` must touch their version. Only the comparator operators (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`, `=`) allow whitespace, so `~ 1.2.3` is invalid.\n- **Empty `||` branch:** an empty branch such as `1.0.0 ||` matches any version, like an empty range.\n- **Prerelease identifiers:** numeric identifiers with leading zeros are accepted, because the spec only forbids leading zeros in MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
